    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated. A levonorgestrel intrauterine system was placed today at her choice, after counseling: lithium carries a small added risk of heart defects in a baby exposed early in pregnancy, valproate is avoided, and any future pregnancy should be planned with psychiatry. The device does not interact with lithium or aripiprazole. [S]<list><item>Condoms as well with new partners, for infection protection.</item><item>Folic acid 0.4 mg daily.</item><item>Mild cramping expected for a few days; call for fever, severe pain, or if she cannot feel the strings.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Bipolar I disorder with psychotic features, in full remission (F31.74)</content>. Remission continues on lithium and aripiprazole. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline are in her phone, and she has no firearm. She chose to write a psychiatric advance directive today. [S]<list><item>Continue lithium carbonate 300 mg twice daily and aripiprazole 10 mg daily.</item><item>Six-month review in six weeks with lithium level, kidney and thyroid tests, and the AIMS.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>108/68 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-9 score 3, from 11 at intake; item 9 scored 0</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 1</td></tr><tr><td>Eating and exercise screen</td><td>Completed today</td><td>SCOFF 0 of 5, from 1 at intake; regular periods; dancing about three and a half hours a day with a rest day; BMI 19.1</td></tr><tr><td>Cervical cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Last cytology three years ago was normal; primary HPV test collected today, every five years if negative</td></tr><tr><td>Contraception and pregnancy planning</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Levonorgestrel intrauterine system placed today; counseled that lithium carries a small added risk of heart defects early in pregnancy, that valproate is avoided because of birth defects and effects on a child&apos;s development, and to plan any pregnancy with psychiatry</td></tr><tr><td>Folic acid</td><td>Completed today</td><td>0.4 mg daily started for a person who could become pregnant</td></tr><tr><td>Intimate partner violence screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; she feels safe</td></tr><tr><td>HIV and hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>No result on record; once-in-a-lifetime tests drawn today with her agreement</td></tr><tr><td>Chlamydia and gonorrhea screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Offered because of a new partner; urine test today</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes and cholesterol screening</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Not due by age; fasting glucose 86 mg/dL, A1c 5.1% and lipids normal at the 12-week antipsychotic check; yearly while on aripiprazole</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Discussed; she prefers to wait and will reconsider in the winter</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap six years ago</td></tr><tr><td>HPV vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Series completed in adolescence</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 1930-1931 season [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: U.S. Selected Practice Recommendations for Contraceptive Use, 2024 (2024); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Medical Condition and Other Indication (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: HPV, HIV, hepatitis C, and sexual-health results by phone. Six-month review in six weeks with lithium level, creatinine, TSH, and the AIMS. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 1930-10-26: six-month review: maintenance treatment, lithium monitoring, and movement check. [S]</paragraph></text>

