    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 18 minutes, with her consent. She chose to complete a psychiatric advance directive: if she becomes ill again, she wants her early warning signs (sleeping less, training for hours, racing thoughts) taken seriously at once, to continue lithium, to avoid valproate, to be treated near home, and to have paper and pencils so she can write. She named a health care agent, recorded in the confidential part of the chart and not named here. She chose not to record other treatment preferences today. The directive will be revisited yearly or after any episode. [S]</paragraph></text>

